{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"80.42.240.28","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"73bfdad3239fbff1c7b19e2977ad11e9","RawContent":"@[member=\"LisaAnthonyPoppy\"] love your last post....completely agree with you on that! More people might also come along to share your day if they are not limited to where they have to stay due to budget reasons \u263a\n\n\nMaybeoneday\n\n12 October 2015....waiting confirmation\n\nRoyalton Riviera Cancun, Mexico","Attachments":[],"Id":1886781,"PostDate":1424302319,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"278120\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/278120-lisaanthonypoppy\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">LisaAnthonyPoppy<\/span><\/a> love your last post....completely agree with you on that! More people might also come along to share your day if they are not limited to where they have to stay due to budget reasons \u263a<br><br>\nMaybeoneday<br>\n12 October 2015....waiting confirmation<br>\nRoyalton Riviera Cancun, Mexico\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"shelina_nessa@yahoo.co.uk","IpAddress":"149.254.56.238","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1421807139,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"maybeoneday","Id":281816,"Name":"maybeoneday","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"74.139.45.237","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"368537a12b46138141215239ac927202","RawContent":"@[member=\"maybeoneday\"]\n\nThanks! That was the only way I felt comfortable handling our wedding!","Attachments":[],"Id":1886802,"PostDate":1424343043,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281816\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281816-maybeoneday\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">maybeoneday<\/span><\/a><br>\nThanks! That was the only way I felt comfortable handling our wedding!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"lisananth@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"166.137.101.169","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1401122033,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-278120.jpg?_r=1421810202","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"LisaAnthonyPoppy","Id":278120,"Name":"LisaAnthonyPoppy","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"75.155.94.124","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"ad5dc583376b4aa24273e238a723872f","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"nattiegams325\"] such a good response.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;You can totally spend as little or as much as you want so it is hard to say what an average cost is. From what other brides have said it I think a realistic budget could be &amp;nbsp;$15000-17000 with about 35-40 guests. This won&#039;t get you many luxuries but it will be a nice wedding :), depending on the resort you choose. Of course it can go much higher than that depending on what details you want to add and whether you have more guests.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I agree that you need to make a list of \"must haves\" and then search for hotels that have the most items from that list. For example, we knew we needed a family resort, it needed to be relatively close to nightlife and it needed to have venues off the beach for about 50 people. Most importantly, we wanted to pay around $1500-$1600 for trips. After taking that into account there weren&#039;t a lot of resorts left that met all these requirements. A travel agent will be the most help, otherwise trying to go through forums alone can be super overwhelming. A travel agent can give you 2 or 3 resorts to look into based on your preferences and then you can try and do research based on that.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I also agree that you can consider receptions outside of the resort. I really wish we had considered this a bit more before booking.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1886807,"PostDate":1424346009,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"275926\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/275926-nattiegams325\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">nattiegams325<\/span><\/a> such a good response.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>You can totally spend as little or as much as you want so it is hard to say what an average cost is. From what other brides have said it I think a realistic budget could be \u00a0$15000-17000 with about 35-40 guests. This won't get you many luxuries but it will be a nice wedding <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>, depending on the resort you choose. Of course it can go much higher than that depending on what details you want to add and whether you have more guests.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I agree that you need to make a list of \"must haves\" and then search for hotels that have the most items from that list. For example, we knew we needed a family resort, it needed to be relatively close to nightlife and it needed to have venues off the beach for about 50 people. Most importantly, we wanted to pay around $1500-$1600 for trips. After taking that into account there weren't a lot of resorts left that met all these requirements. A travel agent will be the most help, otherwise trying to go through forums alone can be super overwhelming. A travel agent can give you 2 or 3 resorts to look into based on your preferences and then you can try and do research based on that.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I also agree that you can consider receptions outside of the resort. I really wish we had considered this a bit more before booking.\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359748704,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1442890536","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"74.139.45.237","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1424363734,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"49eb03e8dd6b7b7591071b99c717b0ba","RawContent":"My wedding costs, not including travel expenses bc that is not wedding exclusively, not including rings or dress, is running me 8k and that&#039;s including private club, officiant, open bar,2 course plated filet mignon or salmon, lots of canap\u00e9s, dj for ceremony, cocktail hour, reception, LED dance floor to make the large space seem much cozier and inviting place to dance, wedding cake from an amazing bakery, chocolate fountain with treats, florist, photographer for day of AND TTD session, makeup artist, daughter and son&#039;s outfits, and decor.\n\nHow I cut costs-\n\nChose a venue that had NO rental fees, used on site WC. Created my menu and priced it out, carefully chose bar package, sought out all vendors worked on prices, bought all my decor from various stores at home and am carefully bubble wrapping and bringing, am hiring a florist for tall centerpieces and bouquet bc mine is very specific with anemones and ranunculus and DIY the other small arrangements,  not having an alter but marrying inside circle of flowers placed in sand, and the venue has all tables, chairs linens, glassware, we are bringing overlays and chargers, lots of candles.\n\n\nI&#039;m very detailed and have high expectations and I literally created it all for 8k. \n\n\nMy vendors are \n\nOfficiant - Petra Rattue personable, woman who I feel like I know already \n\nVenue - Kool Beach \n\nBaker - Carla Molina of Pasteleria la Migaja who is excellent!\n\nPhotographer - Gonzalo Nunez so kind and quick to reply, worked with me on my schedule and had no prerequisites how the time had to be split or started.\n\nDJ - Audio Cancun (amazing so professional excellent ears for matching music based on preferences)\n\nFlorist - Floreria Iris, quick to reply quoted me honestly lots of experience, there are a few good ones but I chose them.\n\nMUA- the oh so fashion forward makeup artist Zoe Elizabeth. So dynamic and creative portfolio, awesome chick.\n\nWe will be buying extra flowers for ceremony and extra petals and small arrangements at Walmart, DAC, and maybe Iris.\n\nDaughters flower girl dress -etsy\n\nSons tux - Calvin Klein on amazon.\n\nBoth outfits totaled less than $180. \n\n\nIf you negotiate, look for honest vendors, and do your research you can have a wedding for as much or as little as you want and it WILL be beautiful. If I had a little more jingle in my el pocketo I would sit back and let everyone do more things for me which would be fabulous, but even with a tight budget and having to wait almost 2 years to save, I never thought I would have to sacrifice things, meant a little more elbow grease on my end. \n\nI don&#039;t like to mention costs or private stuff but people need to know it can be done for far less than 10k. \n\nBam! Lol\n30 guests.","Attachments":[],"Id":1886839,"PostDate":1424363889,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                My wedding costs, not including travel expenses bc that is not wedding exclusively, not including rings or dress, is running me 8k and that's including private club, officiant, open bar,2 course plated filet mignon or salmon, lots of canap\u00e9s, dj for ceremony, cocktail hour, reception, LED dance floor to make the large space seem much cozier and inviting place to dance, wedding cake from an amazing bakery, chocolate fountain with treats, florist, photographer for day of AND TTD session, makeup artist, daughter and son's outfits, and decor.<br>\nHow I cut costs-<br>\nChose a venue that had NO rental fees, used on site WC. Created my menu and priced it out, carefully chose bar package, sought out all vendors worked on prices, bought all my decor from various stores at home and am carefully bubble wrapping and bringing, am hiring a florist for tall centerpieces and bouquet bc mine is very specific with anemones and ranunculus and DIY the other small arrangements,  not having an alter but marrying inside circle of flowers placed in sand, and the venue has all tables, chairs linens, glassware, we are bringing overlays and chargers, lots of candles.<br><br>\nI'm very detailed and have high expectations and I literally created it all for 8k. <br><br>\nMy vendors are <br>\nOfficiant - Petra Rattue personable, woman who I feel like I know already <br>\nVenue - Kool Beach <br>\nBaker - Carla Molina of Pasteleria la Migaja who is excellent!<br>\nPhotographer - Gonzalo Nunez so kind and quick to reply, worked with me on my schedule and had no prerequisites how the time had to be split or started.<br>\nDJ - Audio Cancun (amazing so professional excellent ears for matching music based on preferences)<br>\nFlorist - Floreria Iris, quick to reply quoted me honestly lots of experience, there are a few good ones but I chose them.<br>\nMUA- the oh so fashion forward makeup artist Zoe Elizabeth. So dynamic and creative portfolio, awesome chick.<br>\nWe will be buying extra flowers for ceremony and extra petals and small arrangements at Walmart, DAC, and maybe Iris.<br>\nDaughters flower girl dress -etsy<br>\nSons tux - Calvin Klein on amazon.<br>\nBoth outfits totaled less than $180. <br><br>\nIf you negotiate, look for honest vendors, and do your research you can have a wedding for as much or as little as you want and it WILL be beautiful. If I had a little more jingle in my el pocketo I would sit back and let everyone do more things for me which would be fabulous, but even with a tight budget and having to wait almost 2 years to save, I never thought I would have to sacrifice things, meant a little more elbow grease on my end. <br>\nI don't like to mention costs or private stuff but people need to know it can be done for far less than 10k. <br>\nBam! Lol<br \/>30 guests. \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"lisananth@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"166.137.101.169","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1401122033,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-278120.jpg?_r=1421810202","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"LisaAnthonyPoppy","Id":278120,"Name":"LisaAnthonyPoppy","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"209.91.107.150","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5468912619df9f35a5ce6004ae3cb62b","RawContent":"[quote name=\"LisaAnthonyPoppy\" post=\"1886839\" timestamp=\"1424378289\"]\nMy wedding costs, not including travel expenses bc that is not wedding exclusively, not including rings or dress, is running me 8k and that&#039;s including private club, officiant, open bar,2 course plated filet mignon or salmon, lots of canap\u00e9s, dj for ceremony, cocktail hour, reception, LED dance floor to make the large space seem much cozier and inviting place to dance, wedding cake from an amazing bakery, chocolate fountain with treats, florist, photographer for day of AND TTD session, makeup artist, daughter and son&#039;s outfits, and decor.\nHow I cut costs-\nChose a venue that had NO rental fees, used on site WC. Created my menu and priced it out, carefully chose bar package, sought out all vendors worked on prices, bought all my decor from various stores at home and am carefully bubble wrapping and bringing, am hiring a florist for tall centerpieces and bouquet bc mine is very specific with anemones and ranunculus and DIY the other small arrangements,  not having an alter but marrying inside circle of flowers placed in sand, and the venue has all tables, chairs linens, glassware, we are bringing overlays and chargers, lots of candles.\n\nI&#039;m very detailed and have high expectations and I literally created it all for 8k. \n\nMy vendors are \nOfficiant - Petra Rattue personable, woman who I feel like I know already \nVenue - Kool Beach \nBaker - Carla Molina of Pasteleria la Migaja who is excellent!\nPhotographer - Gonzalo Nunez so kind and quick to reply, worked with me on my schedule and had no prerequisites how the time had to be split or started.\nDJ - Audio Cancun (amazing so professional excellent ears for matching music based on preferences)\nFlorist - Floreria Iris, quick to reply quoted me honestly lots of experience, there are a few good ones but I chose them.\nMUA- the oh so fashion forward makeup artist Zoe Elizabeth. So dynamic and creative portfolio, awesome chick.\nWe will be buying extra flowers for ceremony and extra petals and small arrangements at Walmart, DAC, and maybe Iris.\nDaughters flower girl dress -etsy\nSons tux - Calvin Klein on amazon.\nBoth outfits totaled less than $180. \n\nIf you negotiate, look for honest vendors, and do your research you can have a wedding for as much or as little as you want and it WILL be beautiful. If I had a little more jingle in my el pocketo I would sit back and let everyone do more things for me which would be fabulous, but even with a tight budget and having to wait almost 2 years to save, I never thought I would have to sacrifice things, meant a little more elbow grease on my end. \nI don&#039;t like to mention costs or private stuff but people need to know it can be done for far less than 10k. \nBam! Lol\n30 guests.[\/quote]Ohh ok yeah. If we&#039;re talking about just the wedding , without counting trips, ring, dress, grooms suit, gifts, etc a wedding in Mexico can be well under 10k. Agreed. It&#039;s those little details that really bring the costs up, but it always depends on you and how you allocate costs. \n\nI think you can make any budget work, you might have to give up some things, invite less people, etc. but in the end you can make it work [emoji6]. Whatever your budget is, make sure you leave room for unexpected costs, they always seem to come up and it&#039;s better to be prepared [emoji4]\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1886851,"PostDate":1424366638,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>LisaAnthonyPoppy, on 19 February 2015 - 04:38 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>My wedding costs, not including travel expenses bc that is not wedding exclusively, not including rings or dress, is running me 8k and that's including private club, officiant, open bar,2 course plated filet mignon or salmon, lots of canap\u00e9s, dj for ceremony, cocktail hour, reception, LED dance floor to make the large space seem much cozier and inviting place to dance, wedding cake from an amazing bakery, chocolate fountain with treats, florist, photographer for day of AND TTD session, makeup artist, daughter and son's outfits, and decor.<br>\nHow I cut costs-<br>\nChose a venue that had NO rental fees, used on site WC. Created my menu and priced it out, carefully chose bar package, sought out all vendors worked on prices, bought all my decor from various stores at home and am carefully bubble wrapping and bringing, am hiring a florist for tall centerpieces and bouquet bc mine is very specific with anemones and ranunculus and DIY the other small arrangements,  not having an alter but marrying inside circle of flowers placed in sand, and the venue has all tables, chairs linens, glassware, we are bringing overlays and chargers, lots of candles.<br><br>\nI'm very detailed and have high expectations and I literally created it all for 8k. <br><br>\nMy vendors are <br>\nOfficiant - Petra Rattue personable, woman who I feel like I know already <br>\nVenue - Kool Beach <br>\nBaker - Carla Molina of Pasteleria la Migaja who is excellent!<br>\nPhotographer - Gonzalo Nunez so kind and quick to reply, worked with me on my schedule and had no prerequisites how the time had to be split or started.<br>\nDJ - Audio Cancun (amazing so professional excellent ears for matching music based on preferences)<br>\nFlorist - Floreria Iris, quick to reply quoted me honestly lots of experience, there are a few good ones but I chose them.<br>\nMUA- the oh so fashion forward makeup artist Zoe Elizabeth. So dynamic and creative portfolio, awesome chick.<br>\nWe will be buying extra flowers for ceremony and extra petals and small arrangements at Walmart, DAC, and maybe Iris.<br>\nDaughters flower girl dress -etsy<br>\nSons tux - Calvin Klein on amazon.<br>\nBoth outfits totaled less than $180. <br><br>\nIf you negotiate, look for honest vendors, and do your research you can have a wedding for as much or as little as you want and it WILL be beautiful. If I had a little more jingle in my el pocketo I would sit back and let everyone do more things for me which would be fabulous, but even with a tight budget and having to wait almost 2 years to save, I never thought I would have to sacrifice things, meant a little more elbow grease on my end. <br>\nI don't like to mention costs or private stuff but people need to know it can be done for far less than 10k. <br>\nBam! Lol<br>\n30 guests.<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nOhh ok yeah. If we're talking about just the wedding , without counting trips, ring, dress, grooms suit, gifts, etc a wedding in Mexico can be well under 10k. Agreed. It's those little details that really bring the costs up, but it always depends on you and how you allocate costs. <br><br>\nI think you can make any budget work, you might have to give up some things, invite less people, etc. but in the end you can make it work [emoji6]. Whatever your budget is, make sure you leave room for unexpected costs, they always seem to come up and it's better to be prepared [emoji4]<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359748704,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1442890536","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"74.139.45.237","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1424367468,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"6d3ff0928d7fadef15d79a504bd64b40","RawContent":"Agreed. And I didn&#039;t include travel or lodging bc that&#039;s not actually the \"wedding\". Also the ring and dress can be included I guess but I think those are personal expenses that I didn&#039;t include in my budget although my dress was only $500. I was only referring to the event, but gosh I guess you could have an 8k wedding and blow another 7k on dresses and jewelry if that&#039;s your thing! :)\n\nI know I&#039;ll be saving a little room in my budget for some yummy tropical drinks! This cold weather stinks!","Attachments":[],"Id":1886855,"PostDate":1424367442,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Agreed. And I didn't include travel or lodging bc that's not actually the \"wedding\". Also the ring and dress can be included I guess but I think those are personal expenses that I didn't include in my budget although my dress was only $500. I was only referring to the event, but gosh I guess you could have an 8k wedding and blow another 7k on dresses and jewelry if that's your thing! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><br>\nI know I'll be saving a little room in my budget for some yummy tropical drinks! This cold weather stinks!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"lisananth@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"166.137.101.169","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1401122033,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-278120.jpg?_r=1421810202","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"LisaAnthonyPoppy","Id":278120,"Name":"LisaAnthonyPoppy","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.53.13.68","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e9321105abc1f64c1d6373bded9d7c30","RawContent":"[quote name=\"TinkerSofi\" post=\"1886851\" timestamp=\"1424381038\"]\nOhh ok yeah. If we&#039;re talking about just the wedding , without counting trips, ring, dress, grooms suit, gifts, etc a wedding in Mexico can be well under 10k. Agreed. It&#039;s those little details that really bring the costs up, but it always depends on you and how you allocate costs.\n\nI think you can make any budget work, you might have to give up some things, invite less people, etc. but in the end you can make it work [emoji6]. Whatever your budget is, make sure you leave room for unexpected costs, they always seem to come up and it&#039;s better to be prepared [emoji4]\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk[\/quote]Yea.. My wedding is costing me 7k (not including rings, dress etc) and i&#039;m having it on a resort and getting all of the decor etc that I want.\nI&#039;ve cut costs in areas where certain things aren&#039;t overly necessary or on my immediate wish list, but I don&#039;t think that all resorts are more expensive than having a wedding in a private space. Plus, I really love that i&#039;m going to be spending an entire week with all of my friends\/family with unlimited private events at the resort (Welcome dinner, Rehearsal Dinner &amp;amp; Ceremony\/Reception).","Attachments":[],"Id":1886870,"PostDate":1424372296,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>TinkerSofi, on 19 February 2015 - 05:23 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Ohh ok yeah. If we're talking about just the wedding , without counting trips, ring, dress, grooms suit, gifts, etc a wedding in Mexico can be well under 10k. Agreed. It's those little details that really bring the costs up, but it always depends on you and how you allocate costs.<br><br>\nI think you can make any budget work, you might have to give up some things, invite less people, etc. but in the end you can make it work [emoji6]. Whatever your budget is, make sure you leave room for unexpected costs, they always seem to come up and it's better to be prepared [emoji4]<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>Yea.. My wedding is costing me 7k (not including rings, dress etc) and i'm having it on a resort and getting all of the decor etc that I want.<\/p>\n<p>I've cut costs in areas where certain things aren't overly necessary or on my immediate wish list, but I don't think that all resorts are more expensive than having a wedding in a private space. Plus, I really love that i'm going to be spending an entire week with all of my friends\/family with unlimited private events at the resort (Welcome dinner, Rehearsal Dinner & Ceremony\/Reception).\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>\u00a0<br><br><span style=\"color:#808080;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">My planning thread :<\/span><\/span><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><br><br>\n\u00a0","Email":"perianjohnson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1419423414,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"perianjay","Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"74.139.45.237","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1424374835,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c2b250ad2e36c3653ba1414c82492c9c","RawContent":"Ya too bad my family can&#039;t afford an all inclusive resort. \n\nWe&#039;d be having all the unlimited events on the side of the street in the middle of town, maybe on a small patch of grass if we all has to stay at hotel. Haha! \n\nLove them though!\n\n\n I was trying to rent a big 10 bedroom house and prepare meals ourselves each day, but no one could get deposit together.","Attachments":[],"Id":1886879,"PostDate":1424374636,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Ya too bad my family can't afford an all inclusive resort. <br>\nWe'd be having all the unlimited events on the side of the street in the middle of town, maybe on a small patch of grass if we all has to stay at hotel. Haha! <br>\nLove them though!<br><br>\n I was trying to rent a big 10 bedroom house and prepare meals ourselves each day, but no one could get deposit together.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"lisananth@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"166.137.101.169","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1401122033,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-278120.jpg?_r=1421810202","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"LisaAnthonyPoppy","Id":278120,"Name":"LisaAnthonyPoppy","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"75.155.94.124","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e7060d59b87f038c36a12318a790b7e7","RawContent":"[quote name=\"LisaAnthonyPoppy\" post=\"1886879\" timestamp=\"1424389036\"]\nYa too bad my family can&#039;t afford an all inclusive resort.\nWe&#039;d be having all the unlimited events on the side of the street in the middle of town, maybe on a small patch of grass if we all has to stay at hotel. Haha!\nLove them though!\n\nI was trying to rent a big 10 bedroom house and prepare meals ourselves each day, but no one could get deposit together.[\/quote]I&#039;m sure you guys will have a great time and make amazing memories regardless :). My whole life we&#039;ve gone in groups to coastal cities (not at all inclusives) and we&#039;d just meet up at the beach every day and then plan outings for those that wanted to come. It&#039;s a lot of fun too! and because none of you are really \"attached\" to a resort, then it gives everyone more freedom to go and see different places.","Attachments":[],"Id":1886885,"PostDate":1424376049,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>LisaAnthonyPoppy, on 19 February 2015 - 07:37 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Ya too bad my family can't afford an all inclusive resort.<br>\nWe'd be having all the unlimited events on the side of the street in the middle of town, maybe on a small patch of grass if we all has to stay at hotel. Haha!<br>\nLove them though!<br><br>\nI was trying to rent a big 10 bedroom house and prepare meals ourselves each day, but no one could get deposit together.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>I'm sure you guys will have a great time and make amazing memories regardless <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>. My whole life we've gone in groups to coastal cities (not at all inclusives) and we'd just meet up at the beach every day and then plan outings for those that wanted to come. It's a lot of fun too! and because none of you are really \"attached\" to a resort, then it gives everyone more freedom to go and see different places.\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<br><p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;31;484\/st\/20150813\/e\/Wedding+time%21+\/dt\/-2\/k\/b92c\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\">\u00a0","Email":"sblopezb@gmail.com","IpAddress":"172.219.193.22","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1359748704,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1442890536","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"TinkerSofi","Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":3,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"0acf6c51674bbd994d6c5b08421f80e5","RawContent":"And just traveling with friends and family rocks. People can&#039;t stop talking about it on FB. People made new friends for life.  It&#039;s almost like a once in a lifetime to be able to do that - wedding is the excuse - and I am sooooooo glad we did it!!!! Tearing up lol\n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1886895,"PostDate":1424380354,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                And just traveling with friends and family rocks. People can't stop talking about it on FB. People made new friends for life.  It's almost like a once in a lifetime to be able to do that - wedding is the excuse - and I am sooooooo glad we did it!!!! Tearing up lol<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399414202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":37,"TotalPages":4,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":20,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":30},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
